From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 17:18:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: meson-sm1-odroid-hc4: run the SPI NOR at 40 MHz

At the 104 MHz this node asks for, reads come back corrupted: the first
byte of a transfer has bit 0 flipped from 0 to 1 part of the time, while
the same byte read second in a transfer is always correct.  Reading one
4 KiB block a hundred times returned the wrong contents 157 times, always
the same wrong variant.  Writes are unaffected.

The damage is not academic: flashcp verifies as it goes, so installing a
bootloader erases blocks it should have skipped and can abort halfway,
leaving the flash half written.

Hardkernel's own device tree for this board runs the flash at 40 MHz.
At that rate the same tests come back clean - two hundred block reads
with no mismatch, and repeated flashcp runs with nothing erased.

Tested on ODROID-HC4 with an XT25F128B.

Signed-off-by: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts
@@ -146,11 +146,11 @@ &spifc {
 	flash@0 {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <1>;
 		compatible = "jedec,spi-nor";
 		reg = <0>;
-		spi-max-frequency = <104000000>;
+		spi-max-frequency = <40000000>;
 	};
 };
 
 &usb {
 	phys = <&usb2_phy0>, <&usb2_phy1>;
